From 11b9e5ed336c51a35f43cf9ec438023b2e0ca277 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 15:11:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] fix: 1.4.0 QA round 2 (test-runner errors, template
 over-masking, lossless fold)

Adversarial review of the 1.4.0 surfaces (agent_formats, folding, log
templates, helpers) with fuzzing and a differential against 1.3.0:

- test-runner reduction no longer drops errors printed around or inside a
  run (pytest rule lines in captured output, compiler/make/tox, cargo, npm)
- quoted values and paths are masked in log templates only when they hold a
  digit, so distinct messages and errors are not merged
- zero-count phrases no longer negate a failure line
- recursion markers are found inside JSON tool payloads
- fold_lossless JSON minify is byte-exact for literals; briefs escape
  surrogates and bidi controls; fold idempotence and CR-run fixes
- content_hint="code" on numbered reads; 4300-digit integer crash

Suite 1125 passed, 3 skipped; run_battery 15/15 and threshold_sweep
unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01S4NKzUk5qwpQGbt2YF3Qh3
